Object.assign(entries,{"functionproduct": ["Function-field norm/valuation product formula", "Construct actual integral closures at finite places and infinity for finite separable L/k(t); the total principal order sum is zero.", "Integral closures, finiteness, Dedekind properties, normalized DVR valuation and actual norm identities are proved. Arbitrary characteristic is allowed; the chosen parameter extension must be separable. Identifying the infinity residue field with k and the constructed places with a supplied complete Scheme curve remains open.", ["Actual finite separable L/k(t); characteristic zero is not required.", "Integral closures and their finiteness are constructed, not assumed finite-chart existence."], [["Construct integral closures", "Normalize k[t] and the actual infinity DVR in L."], ["Normalize infinity", "Prove the actual normalized DVR valuation equals inftyValuation."], ["Count via norms", "Add the finite and infinity norm/order identities."], ["Conclude zero", "Use the actual P¹ principal-degree-zero theorem."]]], "cartiercurve": ["Actual Cartier curve restriction and order positivity", "Restrict actual Cartier equations and sum their finite local orders. Effective restrictions are nonnegative, strictly positive when the support is met; constructed effective real decompositions obey the same signs.", "Uses actual Scheme stalks and DVR orders, without assumed ambient dominance or intersection positivity. Original real weights may be negative. A Cartier divisor containing the curve is moved by an actual principal divisor before restriction. Degree independence under moves/arbitrary real presentations and geometric ample positivity remain open.", ["An actual integral curve C, integral ambient X and arbitrary Scheme morphism. Order sums require a normal locally Noetherian quasi-compact C.", "Effective positivity requires the curve not be contained in support; the real case uses a constructed effective decomposition.", "Moving restriction works without avoiding the original support. Independence of its degree from the move is not yet proved."], [["Actual order sum", "Finite actual Cartier coefficients define the local-order sum."], ["Non-dominant restriction", "Generic stalk units give actual curve equations and transition data."], ["Effectivity and full support", "Construct regular equations and prove full inverse-image support."], ["Positivity", "Sum actual nonnegative orders; nonempty support supplies a positive one."], ["Arbitrary original real weights", "Construct an effective decomposition and restrict its positive-weight terms."], ["Principal move", "Subtract one actual local equation to avoid the curve generic image, preserving transition units."]]], "separablenorm": ["Actual norms and principal-divisor pushforward", "In a finite separable Dedekind extension, div(N(a))=h_*div(a), using actual orders and residue degrees.", "Ideal norms and principal norm identities for integral elements and arbitrary function-field units are proved. Separability is required for the extension itself; the base fraction field need not be perfect. Arbitrary characteristic is allowed. The separate point-length pullback formula includes inseparable degree.", ["Actual finite torsion-free Dedekind extension and separable function-field extension.", "A nonzero function and actual height-one points; pushforward weights are residue degrees."], [["Actual ideal norms", "Compute prime-power orders and prove the integral norm identity."], ["Pass to fractions", "Use nonzero numerator and denominator with additive orders."], ["Actual function fields", "Transport through actual fraction-field equivalences and norm compatibility."], ["Take degree", "Actual pushforward preserves residue-weighted degree."]]], "ratproduct": ["Actual principal-divisor degree zero on P¹", "The weighted degree at actual prime points of k[t] plus the actual infinity valuation order is zero.", "Finite places use actual prime points, DVR orders and residue degrees, rather than only formal factor-degree sums. Arbitrary base fields and characteristics are allowed. Normalization of the actual infinity DVR is also proved.", ["An arbitrary field k and nonzero a in k(t).", "Degree uses actual prime-point Finsupp and quotient residue-field finrank."], [["Point degree", "An irreducible prime point has residue degree equal to polynomial degree."], ["Finite principal degree", "The actual weighted finite order sum equals intDegree."], ["Cancel infinity", "The actual negative intDegree at infinity cancels finite degree."]]], "intersection": ["Actual intersections and positivity", "For complete curves contracted by f, relative nefness of −D gives D·C≤0; relative ampleness of −E must give E·C<0. Effective-divisor order signs are now constructed.", "Actual finite Cartier order sums, non-dominant restriction and effective nonnegative/strictly positive degree are proved, including constructed effective real decompositions. Actual complete-curve principal degree zero, independence under moves/presentations, real linearity and geometric relative ample positivity remain open. Geometric ampleness is not redefined as a numerical condition.", ["Proved: actual effective Cartier restriction has nonnegative order sum, strictly positive on meeting support. Constructed effective real decompositions have the same signs.", "Open: identify actual complete-curve Scheme points with constructed places to prove principal-move and presentation independence.", "C must be a complete f-contracted curve. Relative nef signs are definitional; geometric f-ample degree positivity still needs connection."], [["Actual restriction and orders: proved", "Use actual generic units and stalk maps; the ambient map need not be dominant."], ["Effective real decomposition: proved", "Decompose arbitrary original real weights into effective positive-weight Cartier terms."], ["Curve inside support: moving proved", "Subtract an actual local-equation principal divisor and then restrict. Degree independence under this move remains open."], ["Still to connect", "Complete-curve principal degree/presentation independence and strict geometric relative ample degree."]]], "projection": ["Geometric curve projection formula", "Prove (π*D)·Γ=D·π_*[Γ], yielding relative nefness of −π*D.", "Uses the agreed direct divisor/local-order route. Actual finite-divisor pullback, norm/valuation product formula, non-dominant Cartier restriction and moving are proved. Identify constructed places with actual complete normal curve points, prove move/presentation independence and global pullback degree, then connect normalization and point-image degree zero. The full geometric projection formula is still open.", ["Proved: actual point tensor lengths, finite-divisor pullback degree, principal compatibility and function-field norm/valuation formula.", "Proved: actual Cartier curve restriction, finite local-order sum, effective signs and principal moving.", "Open: actual complete Scheme-curve place identification, move independence, global degree pullback and the point-image zero case."], [["Commutative square: proved", "Module pullback and direct Cartier restriction are constructed."], ["Point counting: proved", "Actual tensor lengths prove finite-divisor pullback degree, including inseparability."], ["Norms and valuations: proved", "Construct finite/infinity integral closures and prove their function-field principal product formula."], ["Actual Cartier restriction: proved", "Move local equations off the curve generic image and construct actual restricted equations."], ["Global geometry: open", "Identify actual curve points, prove move-independent degree and global pullback degree, then handle normalization and point images."]]]});

// Hartshorne I.6 and actual residue-degree bridge: formal-20
Object.assign(entries,{"infinityresidue": ["Infinity residue field and actual base-field degrees", "The actual infinity DVR of k(t) has residue field k. Over an algebraically closed base field, the constructed infinity points have residue degree one.", "Leading-term cancellation approximates every infinity-regular function by an actual constant modulo the maximal ideal. Finite and infinity weights now use the same field k. No finite-type k-algebra assumption is imposed on the infinity ring.", ["An arbitrary field k and the actual valuation subring of inftyValuation.", "Degree-one infinity residues require IsAlgClosed k; arbitrary characteristic is allowed."], [["Approximate by a constant", "Leading-term cancellation gives positive order at infinity."], ["Actual residue field", "Prove bijectivity of the actual constant-to-residue map."], ["Unify base-field weights", "Use the actual residue-degree tower to identify the pushforward coefficient with k-degree."], ["Algebraically closed field", "Finite residue-field extensions have degree one."]]], "curvecenters": ["Hartshorne I.6: unique valuation center", "For a proper normal integral curve C, a function-field valuation ring A containing the ground-field constants has a unique actual map Spec A→C extending the generic point. Its local stalk map is an isomorphism; a nontrivial A has a closed-point center.", "The base-field map, valuative square, unique lift and local-ring isomorphism are all constructed. Normality and dimension imply that each stalk is a field or DVR. A local inclusion of valuation rings in the same fraction field is an isomorphism. No center existence or stalk compatibility is assumed.", ["An actual integral locally Noetherian Scheme C, integrally closed stalks and krullDim C≤1.", "The structure map C→Spec k is proper; A is a valuation subring of the actual function field containing its actual constants."], [["Actual ground-field map", "Extract k→K(C) from the generic-point structure map."], ["Unique proper lift", "Construct the square and apply the verified valuative criterion."], ["Same function field", "Prove actual compatibility of the center stalk map and valuation inclusion."], ["Local-ring isomorphism", "Normal curve stalks are fields or DVRs; the local map is bijective."], ["Closed center", "A generic center would force A to be the whole function field; codimension-one curve points are closed."]]], "curveplaces": ["Hartshorne I.6: closed-point/valuation bijection", "The actual codimension-one closed points of a proper normal integral curve correspond bijectively to nontrivial ground-field valuation rings in its actual function field.", "Point→valuation uses the image of the actual DVR stalk in the function field. Valuation→point uses the unique proper center. Equality and uniqueness in both directions are verified. Classification by finite/infinity integral-closure primes remains to be connected; global curve degree is not yet complete.", ["An actual normal integral locally Noetherian C of dimension≤1 with proper C→Spec k.", "Valuation rings lie in actual K(C), are nontrivial and contain actual ground-field constants. No characteristic restriction."], [["Construct actual point valuations", "Use the DVR stalk image; a uniformizer has no regular inverse."], ["Ground-field constants", "Prove membership from the actual specialization square."], ["Identify the center subring", "The actual stalk isomorphism gives equality with A."], ["Uniqueness", "Canonical point lifts coincide with the unique proper lift."], ["Bijection", "The actual constructions prove both injectivity and surjectivity."]]], "curveorders": ["Actual curve-center correspondence preserves orders", "A DVR place of the actual function field has a unique closed-point center on a proper normal curve, and the correspondence preserves the actual local order of every nonzero rational function.", "Proved from the actual center stalk isomorphism, function-field compatibility and arbitrary numerator/denominator representatives. Order preservation is not assumed. Finite/infinity place classification and transport of the total order sum remain open.", ["An actual proper normal integral curve C of dimension≤1 over Spec k.", "A is a nontrivial actual DVR subring containing constants; its center and stalk isomorphism are outputs."], [["Orders in the same fraction field", "Actual DVR isomorphisms preserve orders of arbitrary rational functions."], ["Actual Scheme center", "Use the constructed stalk isomorphism to identify curve orders."], ["Unique center and all orders", "Output the actual closed point, uniqueness and all local-order identities together."]]]});
